# ⛔ 6.7.10 (ops-5) — A WHOLE DEREFERENCE AS AN ADDRESS-PASSED ARGUMENT PASSES ITS POINTER (the user's
# decision 6: `*p` is a struct value at every size). `take(*p)`, `take((*p))`, `take(*gp())`, `take(*w.ps)` into
# a by-value struct parameter over 8 B, or into a `*S` parameter of any size, pushed the word the dereference
