# The parameter takes a tuple's ADDRESS, and the call leaves its values in the return registers —
# nothing to point at — so the value push handed the callee the first value as an address (a
# SIGSEGV, or a silent read through it). Refused by name: bind the values first. Cursor on the
# callee's name; 1 = reported (the caller then pushes the argument as before, the parse in step,
